From 2a09ec837e59f1401de011f42dc27acec20916ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LightMoss <noreply@github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:44:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250-pwm-fan-cooling: poll the fan zone

tsens only interrupts when the temperature crosses a threshold, and
step_wise takes the fan down one trip per evaluation, on a falling reading.
Without polling, the fan can stay at a higher level than the trips call for
after a drop across several trips, or after userspace raises the trip
temperatures (LightMoss's fan modes rewrite them). Poll the zone every two
seconds so the fan always settles where the trips put it.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-pwm-fan-cooling.dtsi | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-pwm-fan-cooling.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-pwm-fan-cooling.dtsi
index 59ce40aec..fbd550991 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-pwm-fan-cooling.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-pwm-fan-cooling.dtsi
@@ -2,9 +2,17 @@
 /*
  * Bind the PWM fan to a thermal zone so the kernel drives it.
  *
+ * The zone is also polled: tsens only interrupts when the temperature
+ * crosses a threshold, and the step_wise governor takes the fan down one
+ * trip per evaluation, and only on a falling reading. Without polling the
+ * fan could stay at a higher level than the trips call for, after a drop
+ * across several trips or after userspace moves the trips up (LightMoss's
+ * fan modes rewrite these trip temperatures).
  */
 
 &{/thermal-zones/cluster1-thermal} {
+	polling-delay = <2000>;
+
 	trips {
 		fan_active0: fan-active0 {
 			temperature = <45000>;
